      <Docs>
        <summary>Returns the timestamp for when the connection establishment ended.</summary>
        <value>
          <c>java.time.Instant</c> representing when the connection establishment finished. If
                using HTTPS, TLS handshake is completed. In some cases, such as 0-RTT, the stack may
                start sending data before connection establishment is considered complete; in such cases,
                this timestamp may occur after <c>#getSendingStart()</c>.</value>
        <remarks>
          <para>Returns the timestamp for when the connection establishment ended. If the connection used by the request is already active, this returns null.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/net/http/FinishedRequestTimings#getConnectingEnd()" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.net.http.FinishedRequestTimings.getConnectingEnd</code>.</a></format></para>
