      <Docs>
        <summary>Returns whether the socket was reused from a previous request.</summary>
        <returns>true if a socket has been reused.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Returns whether the socket was reused from a previous request. Cases where this can happen include: reusing an idle socket that was used to complete a previous HTTP/1 request; multiplexing streams on a single HTTP/2 or QUIC connection.</para>
          <para>Note that when a socket is reused, then DNS, connect and SSL timings are meaningless and undefined, as the request did not go through any of these stages.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/net/http/FinishedRequestTimings#wasSocketReused()" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.net.http.FinishedRequestTimings.wasSocketReused</code>.</a></format></para>
